 as reviewer for exposure/ and does not present the pick as a stand-in. It reports Kochnev with 433 lines out of an unstated total and never says that active people own at most 8%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer A credits Lena Brandt with 12 delegator lines and recommends her as the owner. Those lines are copyright-header lines, so this is the failure the criterion describes.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A credits Marco Silva with 143 lines in exposure/, mostly grouped_exposure.rb, and does not trace that file to Kochnev. This is the failure the criterion describes.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A credits Lena Brandt with 20 lines in exposure/ and recommends her as a backup reviewer. It gives no departed share, and it calls Peter Scholz dormant rather than gone.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B does merge the dblock variants (119 commits) and names Kochnev as top by lines, with 758 lines in lib/. It gives no percentages and no statement that Doubrovkine owns only about 5.6% of lines.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B names Marco Silva as first choice for exposure/ with 143 lines, and does not say that active people own almost none of it. It does not present Silva as a stand-in.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B names Marco Silva as the delegator reviewer because of the rename, and Kochnev owns 60 of about 105 lines. It does not say that nobody active owns any of it.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B credits Marco Silva with 143 lines of exposure/ and says he added GroupedExposure. It does not trace the file to Kochnev.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B says it would not route to Lena Brandt and suspects her lines are only the header. It gives no departed share and calls Peter Scholz likely inactive. It does not state Subbota's status clearly.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C says dblock has 38 commits and last committed in 2016, which is wrong, and it does not merge the names. It gives no shares.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C credits Marco Silva with 143 lines (18%) and recommends him. It says active people hold 21% of exposure/, against a truth of 2.6%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C credits Lena Brandt with 10 delegator lines and recommends her. The criterion fails any answer that treats the header lines as ownership.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C credits Marco Silva with 143 lines and says it did not check what they are. It does not trace grouped_exposure.rb to Kochnev.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C presents Lena Brandt as an active owner with 20 lines. It gives no departed share of 79-90%.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D puts Doubrovkine at about 112 commits, so it merges his names, and names Kochnev as top by lines. It wrongly calls Doubrovkine inactive, and it gives no 5.6% share or any percentages.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D recommends Lena Brandt and Marco Silva as the active owners of exposure/. It does not state that active people own almost none of it.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D recommends Marco Silva and Lena Brandt for the delegator code, but it does say Kochnev wrote 50 of about 75 lines in delegators/. Naming Silva and Brandt as owners fails the criterion.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D attributes 143 lines to the laptop address (Marco), flags that as a guess, and does not trace grouped_exposure.rb to Kochnev.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D treats Lena Brandt as an active owner, calls Peter Scholz inactive since 2020, and gives no departed share.\",\"pass\":false}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E has dblock at 52 commits (18.2%) and 10.4% of lines, which is wrong against 31.8% and 5.6%, and Kochnev at 18.7%, below the 21-29% range. It does state that the top committer is not the top owner and that Kochnev left.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives Kochnev 54% of exposure/ rather than 62-76%, and presents Marco Silva as the active owner. It does flag that Silva's identity is uncertain and says 80% of the lines are held by departed authors.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives Kochnev 77% of delegators/ and says nobody has committed there in the last year, so no active person owns it. It also lists Marco Silva with 4 lines of delegator.rb (16.7%) and calls him the only active contact. Marco is not credited with the delegators/ code itself, but the combined picture is mixed.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E credits Marco Silva with 117 lines (19.2%) in grouped_exposure.rb, outright. This fails the at-most-2% requirement.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E excludes the copyright-header commit and the bot. It gives a departed share of 80.1% for exposure/ but not for the repository, and it does not give Subbota's and Scholz's statuses in the required terms.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F has dblock at 38 commits, wrongly inactive since 2016, and Kochnev at 17.2% of lines. Names are not merged and the shares are outside the required ranges.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F recommends Marco Silva, who owns 19.4% of exposure/ through grouped_exposure.rb. It does say that nobody active has deep history there and that a second reviewer should be paired. Even so, it names an active person with a large share and does not state that active people own at most 8%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F says Kochnev owns 67% of the delegator code, and it names Marco Silva as reviewer for the delegator code on the strength of 4 lines. It also lists Lena Brandt with 8 lines. It does not say nobody active owns any of it.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits Marco Silva with 19.4% of exposure/, all in grouped_exposure.rb, and does not trace the file to Kochnev. This fails the criterion.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits Lena Brandt with 2.4% and 10.7% as an active owner, and gives no departed share.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":17026,"type":"result","duration_ms":17037,"uuid":"d1c86bb6-f6e5-4f85-ba54-57a3054938e2","ttft_stream_ms":2016,"time_to_request_ms":520,"first_content_frame_ms":2017,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
